# gdm -- the greeter, and the last package on the path from a booted kernel to a
# login prompt.
#
# GNOME 48 series, BLFS 12.4, which pins 48.0.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gdm/48/gdm-48.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=1bc06daff093ec7b5e37ecb4f92e5da3474a1b1ba076edb9151ee967d1c30adf
SRC_DIR=gdm-48.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Ddefault-pam-config=lfs, AND THE DEFAULT SHIPS A GREETER THAT REFUSES
# EVERYONE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This is the most dangerous default in the package, because it fails CLOSED and
# fails SILENTLY.
#
# The option is a combo defaulting to 'autodetect'. meson.build:198-220 resolves
# that by probing the BUILD environment for a distribution marker:
#
#     distro_autodetect_map = {
#       '/etc/redhat-release': 'redhat',  '/etc/fedora-release': 'redhat',
#       '/etc/exherbo-release': 'exherbo', '/etc/arch-release': 'arch',
#       '/etc/lfs-release': 'lfs',
#     }
#
# and falls back to the 'distro' option, which defaults to 'none'.
#
# NONE OF THOSE FILES EXIST IN THE DUCT BUILDER. duct-filesystem writes
# /etc/os-release, not /etc/lfs-release. So autodetect resolves to 'none', and
# data/meson.build:136 is
#
#     pam_data_files = pam_data_files_map.get(default_pam_config, [])
#
# -- an EMPTY LIST. No PAM configuration is installed at all, and the build
# succeeds.
#
# linux-pam's `other` stack denies by default, so a gdm with no /etc/pam.d files
# is a greeter that rejects every user, every time, with correct credentials.
# There is no error at build time, no warning, and no missing library: the
# package installs a complete-looking greeter that cannot authenticate anyone.
#
# 'lfs' is a first-class choice in that combo and this IS an LFS-derived system.
# install.sh asserts all five files by name rather than checking the directory,
# because an empty pam.d and a partial one fail the same way and only the
# per-file list can tell them apart.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dsysconfdir=/etc, BECAUSE MESON'S DEFAULT PUTS ALL OF IT IN /usr/etc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# _scripts/build-meson.sh passes --prefix=/usr and nothing else, and meson's
# sysconfdir defaults to `etc` RELATIVE TO THE PREFIX. gdm derives EIGHT paths
# from it -- gdmconfdir (:22), dmconfdir (:23), lang_config_file (:26),
# dbus_sys_dir (:28), pam_prefix (:40), dconf_sysconfig (:228), the SYSCONFDIR
# macro compiled into the daemon (:241), and the applications data (:338).
#
# Left alone, every one of those lands under /usr/etc: the PAM files nothing
# would read, the D-Bus policy nothing would load, and a daemon compiled to look
# for its configuration in a directory no other package writes to. Same trap as
# evolution-data-server's SYSCONF_INSTALL_DIR, reached by a different mechanism
# -- there it was the project's own variable, here it is a meson builtin the
# house script does not set.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dinitial-vt=1, AND BLFS SAYS 7
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This is the one place tonight where the book's value is wrong for this system
# and the upstream DEFAULT is right, so it is set explicitly rather than left
# alone -- the reasoning is worth more than the value.
#
# BLFS passes -D initial-vt=7, which is the traditional X placement: gettys on
# vt1-6, display server on vt7. Duct does not boot that way. duct-live's
# graphical-session searches /usr/sbin/gdm then /usr/bin/gdm and RUNS IT ON
# TTY1, and duct-live's install.sh asserts a two-way edge with console-session
# -- console-session asks `graphical-session --would-start` before taking tty1
# for a shell -- specifically so a shell and a greeter cannot land on the same
# terminal.
#
# So the boot path reserves TTY1 for this greeter. With initial-vt=7, gdm would
# move its greeter to a terminal nothing coordinates while duct-live held tty1
# empty for it. THAT ASSERTION IN duct-live WOULD STILL PASS: it guards which
# script takes tty1, not which VT gdm chooses.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rest
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -Dlogind-provider=elogind: a combo defaulting to 'systemd' (meson.build:129
# vs :140). Duct has elogind, and like gnome-settings-daemon this package names
# it properly rather than reaching it through the libsystemd.pc symlink.
# -Dsystemd-journal=false: defaults TRUE and there is no journald here.
# -Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no and -Dsystemduserunitdir=no: both accept the literal
# 'no', so unlike gnome-session this package CAN decline its units outright and
# nothing has to be removed afterwards.
# -Drun-dir=/run/gdm: BLFS's value, and the one place its command needs no
# adjustment.
# -Dgdm-xsession=false: its default, and BLFS turns it ON. It installs the gdm
# Xsession file for X sessions this desktop does not offer -- mutter here is
# built without X11 and gnome-session's xsessions entry was removed two packages
# ago for the same reason.
# -Dx11-support=false with -Dwayland-support=true: meson.build:46-48 errors if
# BOTH are off, so the pair has to move together.
#
# -Dselinux=disabled, -Dlibaudit=disabled, -Dplymouth=disabled: all three are
# FEATURE options defaulting to 'auto', and none of the three libraries is
# packaged, so all three would resolve off by themselves today. Pinned because
# an auto feature is decided by whatever the seeded build image happens to
# contain, and the image is the union of everything published -- so "off" today
# is a property of the seed rather than a decision.
#
# The gdm user and group are NOT created here. duct-filesystem already carries
# gdm:x:21:21 and group gdm:x:21, so -Duser and -Dgroup keep their defaults.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsysconfdir=/etc \
-Ddefault-pam-config=lfs \
-Dlogind-provider=elogind \
-Dsystemd-journal=false \
-Dsystemdsystemunitdir=no \
-Dsystemduserunitdir=no \
-Dinitial-vt=1 \
-Drun-dir=/run/gdm \
-Dgdm-xsession=false \
-Dwayland-support=true \
-Dx11-support=false \
-Dselinux=disabled \
-Dlibaudit=disabled \
-Dplymouth=disabled"
